1. Problem Statement

Develop a C++ program to represent university departments and their communication links using an adjacency matrix. The program should display the connection status between departments and indicate whether communication links exist between any two departments.

2. Introduction
A university consists of different departments, such as Computer Engineering, Electronics and Telecommunication, Mechanical Engineering, and Civil Engineering. These departments may communicate or share information with each other.
A graph is a data structure used to represent departments and their communication links. In this program, departments are represented as vertices, and communication links are represented as edges. An adjacency matrix is used to store and display the connections between departments in a simple tabular form.

3. Objectives

To understand the concept of graphs and adjacency matrices.

To represent university departments as vertices.

To store communication links between departments.

To display the adjacency matrix.
To check the connection status between any two departments.

4. Short Theory
An adjacency matrix is a two-dimensional array used to represent a graph. If there are  departments, the matrix contains  elements.

1 indicates that a communication link exists between two departments.

0 indicates that no communication link exists.
The diagonal elements are 0 when a department has no link to itself.

For an undirected graph, the adjacency matrix is symmetric because if Department A is connected to Department B, Department B is also connected to Department A.

For example, if Computer Engineering is connected to Electronics Engineering, the corresponding matrix entries are both 1.

5. Algorithm
Start the program.

Read the number of university departments.

Enter the names of all departments.

Initialize the adjacency matrix with zeros.

Read the communication links between departments.

Set the corresponding matrix entries to 1.

Display the adjacency matrix.

Accept two department names from the user.

Check the matrix entry for the selected departments.

Display whether a communication link exists.
Stop the program.

